  "scope": "One disposable Kind cluster and one local-only Python serving fixture (one replica). The fixture accepts a fixed set of benign job IDs, caps waiting depth at two, maps synthetic principals to service classes, orders held work by class, and uses a manually advanced fixture clock to expire one waiting item. All queue receipts and execution records come from the running server process. Calls use localhost inside its Pod; no Service, external endpoint, model, secrets, or live target is involved. Synthetic principal labels exercise class authorization policy only; they are not authenticated identities. This does not validate production authentication, gateway integration, real inference, multi-replica queue coordination, durable receipts, or production timeout semantics.",
